  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Revenue Policy and Administration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve auditor performance, audit management, and audit issue resolution at the Georgia Revenue Service as well as strengthen the interaction between the taxpayer services and audit monitoring functions. A resident audit advisor was posted to Tbilisi in March 2012 and her expertise will be supplemented by intermittent advisors; seven TDYs are scheduled for the remainder of 2012. Two, tax policy subject matter experts who helped to implement the USAID-funded Economic Prosperity Initiative project have been brought under consulting agreements to provide continuity in the project&apos;s assistance. They are working alongside the OTA-Revenue resident advisor, providing technical expertise in audit compliance and in implementing a newly developed audit manual.</narrative>
  </description>
